  +## Updating
  +
  +`cpe update` checks for the latest GitHub release and downloads the appropriate binary if a newer version is available. The update process:
  +
  +- Uses the same verification mechanism as releases (SHA256SUMS)
  +- Downloads the binary (~92 MB) and verifies it
  +- Automatically restarts any running `cpe start` sessions
  +- Can be run with `--check` to only check for newer versions without installing
  +
  +Automatic background update checks occur after each short-lived command (like `cpe status`, `cpe list`, etc.), but only once per 24 hours. To disable automatic checks, set `update_auto: false` in `~/.config/cpe/config.json`. Dev builds are exempt from automatic updates.
  +
   ## Per-repo configuration
   
   The file `cpe.config.json` at the repo root controls how `cpe` behaves for that specific project. On first use `cpe` will prompt you to set it up; you can also run `cpe bootstrap --edit` to open it directly.
